OL,3,AGiant tunnel proposed to clean up
OL,4,AWindermere's sewage problem
OL,5,
OL,6,FA #3.6bn proposal to stop sewage being
OL,7,Fdischarged into Windermere, England's
OL,8,Flargest lake, has been unveiled.
OL,10,FThe plans, which are backed by the
OL,11,Flocal water company United Utilities
OL,12,Fand clean water campaigners, would see
OL,13,Fa tunnel up to 12 miles (19km) long
OL,14,Fbuilt to transport sewage away from the
OL,15,Flake.
OL,17,FAt the moment both raw sewage and
OL,18,Ftreated effluent are discharged into
OL,19,FWindermere and campaigners say that is
OL,20,Fwhy parts of the lake have been turning
OL,21,Fgreen each summer, so-called algal
OL,22,Fblooming.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
